        <ul class="feature-list">
          <li><strong>Vote 1 (Constituency):</strong> Elects a single MSP using First Past the Post. The candidate with the most votes wins.</li>
          <li><strong>Vote 2 (Regional List):</strong> Designed to correct disproportionate outcomes from the constituency vote using the D'Hondt system.</li>
          <li><strong>How D'Hondt Works:</strong> Parties that win many constituency seats are penalised in the regional allocation. Their votes are divided by (seats won + 1).</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="section-text">Understanding this system is not optional if you want to use your vote effectively. The second vote is not a "backup" for your first choice—it's a separate mechanism with its own logic.</p>
